Just two hours in and I am amazed, I was having a mild bout of sleeplesness and this game just pulled me in, like seriously people YOU SHALL get this game. It is not a traditional game and yet what you have learnt in years of gaming can help you with this game - especially in the decision making process - the graphics are very good, maybe they should have applied the Tomb Raider 2013-Engine to get the Tress-FX going, however this game is beautiful and well worth the purchase...
What I like:
Great Story;
Interesting Characters and premise (sofar);
The visuals are beautifully done;
The soundtrack is very well done;
The humor and emotions are very well conveyed and the voice-acting is quite up to standard;
Controller Support!
Some thought went into this game and it shows.
What I do not like:
Graphics are very good yes, but some texture issues and some other graphical bugs are there;
Controller Support is there but the right analog viewing is always "just a little off";
Soundtrack is well done, however in the beginning the same song playing continually starts to get annoying after the first three times it is repeated;
The lip-synching and voices of characters are speaking "Terribly-Out-Of-Sync-English" especially with the subtitles enabled it becomes glaringly obvious how off-cue the lip-synching is;
To rap it up awesome game...MUST BUY THEM ALL!

